************************* Encryption ************************

End to end Encryption

eg whatsapp

me send message ------ my friend
so message is encrypted at me end and then decrypted at friends server end.

Types of Encryption
-Symmetric
-Asymmetric



Symmetric :
so here what happens is that both sender and receiver has a key, using that key the message is encrypted and at receiver end using that same key the message is decrypted.

But this option is not very safe.

in order to make it more safer we go to assymmetric encryption.


Asymmetric :

here we have 2 keys
-Public (which will be with both sender and receiver)
-Private key (this will be only with receiver)


sender->message->public key->encrypted message ->pass encrypted message + public key ----------------  Receiver (take encrypted msg + public key + private msg)

the combination of private ley+public key will be utilized to decrypt the message.

this is very safe.




